SUMMARY:Entrepreneur\, Reverend\, Abolitionist: Stephen Smith's Journey from Columbia to Philadelphia
DESCRIPTION:(left) Presenter Michael Clemmons. (right) A portrait of Stephen Smith.\nOn Thursday\, September 10\, join LancasterHistory as we kick off our fall season of the Regional History Colloquium Series with speaker Michael Clemmons\, who will discuss Entrepreneur\, Reverend\, Abolitionist: Stephen Smith’s Journey From Columbia to Philadelphia. Stephen Smith was a 19th-century African American raised in indentured servitude in Columbia\, PA. He went on to become a leader in the African Methodist Episcopal Church\, an advocate for freedom\, and the richest Black man in America. Michael Clemmons\, former Vice President of the Mother Bethel AME Church Historical Society\, joins us to discuss the life of Stephen Smith\, focusing on his accomplishments and setbacks in his journey from humble beginnings in Lancaster County to Philadelphia and Bethel AME Church. \nMichael Clemmons is a Philadelphia-based public historian\, researcher\, and docent at the Richard Allen Museum. He has collaborated with the Free Library\, the Historical Society of Pennsylvania\, the Philadelphia Athenaeum\, and the African American Museum of Philadelphia. Clemmons is a member and former Vice President of the Mother Bethel AME Church Historical Society and a founding member of the Black Docents Collective. Together with Dr. Donna Rilling\, he co-authored the successful nomination of the historic homes of Stephen Smith and William Whipper for inclusion on the Philadelphia Historical Commission Register of Historic Places. As an independent researcher\, he continues to explore and document their legacies. His perspectives have been featured in the Philadelphia Inquirer Op-Ed page and on the 1838 Black Metropolis© website. Clemmons is a retired aerospace engineering manager and transit rail safety consultant. He holds a B.S. from the University of Pennsylvania and an M.S. from Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University. \nEVENT DETAILS & HOW TO REGISTER \nThis event is expected to take place in person at the LancasterHistory Museum & Research Center on Thursday\, September 10\, 2026. Doors open and the reception begins at 5pm. The lecture will begin at 5:30pm. The lecture will also be streamed to Zoom at 5:30pm for those who wish to join us virtually. \nThis program is free and open to the public. In-person attendance requires advance registration in order to guarantee a seat. Due to capacity restrictions\, tickets may not be available at the door. Virtual attendance requires advance registration in order to receive the Zoom link. Register online by clicking the appropriate link below or by calling 717.392.4633. The online version of this program will also be recorded and uploaded to LancasterHistory’s YouTube channel after the event. \nREGISTER TO ATTEND IN PERSON \nREGISTER TO ATTEND ONLINE \nPlease Note: Your Zoom information will be sent to you in your confirmation email upon registering for the online option. If you do not receive this email and it is not in your junk and spam folders\, please contact support@lancasterhistory.org.
URL:https://stevensandsmithcenter.org/event/stephen-smith/
LOCATION:LancasterHistory Museum & Research Center\, 230 North President Avenue\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17603\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://stevensandsmithcenter.org/wp-content/uploads/Stephen-Smith-Lecture_webFI.avif
